@{
    
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<style>
    body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .bg-welfare-left {
        background-color: #0747AE;
        padding: 15px;
    }

    .bg-welfare-left h3 {
        font-size: 21px;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: #fff;
    }

    .bg-welfare-left ul li {
        margin-top: 18px;
        font-size: 17px;
        color: #fff;
    }

    .bg-welfare-left ul li a {
        color: #fff;
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .bg-welfare-left ul li a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .content-box {
        border: 1px dashed #000;
        background: #fff;
        padding: 20px;
    }

    .welfare-font {
        font-size: 17px;
        color: #000;
        text-align: justify;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    hr {
        border: 1px solid #000;
    }
</style>

<!-- ================= BANNER ================= -->
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-12 p-0"
        style="margin-top:-20px;
        background:url('https://img.freepik.com/premium-photo/extensive-collection-books-library_868797-8212.jpg') center/cover fixed;">
        <div style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.5)">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-center" style="min-height:300px;">
                    <h3 class="display-6 text-white fw-bold text-uppercase">
                        Basic Electrical Engineering Lab
                    </h3>
                    <div class="d-inline-flex text-white">
                        <a href="/" class="text-white text-decoration-none ">Home</a>
                        <i class="fa fa-angle-double-right px-2 pt-1"></i>
                        <span class="text-uppercase">Basic Electrical Engineering Lab</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ================= MAIN CONTENT ================= -->
<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row">
        <style>
            .bg-welfare-left ul li {
                margin-top: 20px;
                font-size: 17px;
                line-height: 1.5;
                color: #fff;
                font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            }

            .bg-welfare-left hr {
                border-bottom: 2px solid white !important;
            }
        </style>
                @Html.Partial("~/Views/Shared/DeptSidebar/_ELE_Sidebar.cshtml")

        <!-- RIGHT CONTENT -->
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <div class="content-box">

                <h2 class="fw-bold" style="color:#0747AE;">Basic Electrical Engineering Lab</h2>
                <hr />
                <div class="row mt-2">
                    
                    <div class="col-sm-7">
                        <p class="welfare-font">
                            The Basic Electrical Engineering Laboratory provides a strong foundation for undergraduate
                            engineering students by offering practical exposure to core electrical engineering
                            principles.
                            Equipped with modern experimental setups, the laboratory enables students to analyze and
                            validate
                            concepts related to DC and AC circuits, electrical machines, transformers, measuring
                            instruments,
                            and basic power systems. Students perform key experiments, including Ohm’s law, Kirchhoff’s
                            laws,
                            network theorems, single- and three-phase circuits, transformer characteristics, DC and AC
                            machines,
                            and electrical measurements, thereby reinforcing theoretical knowledge through hands-on
                            implementation. Emphasis is placed on safe operating practices, precise measurements,
                            circuit
                            analysis, and systematic troubleshooting. The laboratory supports regular practical
                            sessions,
                            
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-lg-5">
                        <img src="~/Content/img/Basic_Electrical_Engineering_Lab.jpg" class="p-1"
                            style="height:350px;width:100%;border:1px dashed #000;object-fit:cover" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="welfare-font m-0 p-0">

                    skill-based training, demonstrations, and introductory project work under the supervision of
                            experienced faculty and technical staff, playing a crucial role in preparing students for
                            advanced
                            studies, industry-oriented learning, and professional practice in electrical engineering.
                    </p>
                </div>


                <p class="welfare-font fw-bold">List of Experiments</p>
                <ul class="welfare-font" style="list-style-type:disc !important;">
                    <li>Verification of Kirchhoff’s laws</li>
                    <li>Measurement of power and power factor in a single-phase ac series inductive circuit, and study
                        the improvement of power factor using a capacitor.</li>
                    <li>Study the phenomenon of resonance in an RLC series circuit and determine the resonant frequency.
                    </li>
                    <li>Connection and measurement of the power consumption of a fluorescent lamp (tube light). </li>
                    <li>Measurement of power in a 3-phase circuit by the two-wattmeter method and determination of its
                        power factor for star as well as delta-connected load.</li>
                    <li>Determination of parameters of an AC single-phase series RLC circuit </li>
                    <li>Determination of (i) Voltage ratio, (ii) polarity, and (iii) efficiency by load test of a
                        single-phase Transformer </li>
                    <li>Determination of the efficiency of a DC shunt motor by load test </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>